problems.problem:
Problem 3. Identification of an organic compound

The molar mass of organic compound $\mathbf{A}$, which shows neither optical nor geometric isomerism and contains no quaternary carbon atom, is $100$. Complete combustion of $100\,\mathrm{mg}$ of this compound gives $372\,\mathrm{mg}$ of a mixture consisting only of carbon dioxide and water. The product of the oxidation of compound $\mathbf{A}$ with $\ce{K2Cr2O7}$ under mild conditions is compound $\mathbf{B}$ with a molar mass of $98$. Compound $\mathbf{A}$ does not react with a solution of bromine in carbon tetrachloride. Give:

a) the molecular formula of compound $\mathbf{A}$;

b) the functional groups present in compounds $\mathbf{A}$ and $\mathbf{B}$;

c) the structural formulae of compounds $\mathbf{A}$ and $\mathbf{B}$.

Molar masses in g/mol: H - 1, C - 12, O - 16.

