d) wzory perspektywiczne Hawortha produktów hydrolizy zmetylowanego disacharydu $\mathbf{IV}$ i $\mathbf{V}$ (w postaci anomerów $\alpha$);

e) wzór perspektywiczny Hawortha disacharydu $\mathbf{I}$.

problems.problem:
Problem 5. A thermolysin inhibitor

Phosphoramidon is a natural inhibitor of the enzyme thermolysin, a protease occurring in unicellular organisms of cold ocean waters.

On the basis of the following data:

1. molecular formula of the disodium salt of phosphoramidon: $\ce{C23H32N3Na2O10P}$;

2. this compound is composed of the dipeptide leucyltryptophan, the monosaccharide L-rhamnose and a phosphoric(V) acid residue;

3. the N-terminus of the dipeptide is bound by an amide (phosphoramide) bond to the phosphate residue;

4. the phosphate group is also bound (by an ester bond) to the monosaccharide;

5. The test for reducing sugars with phosphoramidon is negative;

6. After exhaustive methylation followed by complete hydrolysis of phosphoramidon, 2,3,4-tri-O-methylated L-rhamnose is obtained (and other non-sugar products);

7. Oxidation of the monosaccharide with dilute nitric(V) acid leads to the formation of a carboxylic acid with an unbranched carbon chain of general formula $\ce{C6H12O6}$;

8. In phosphoramidon, in the L-rhamnose unit, the configurations at the individual carbon atoms are identical to those in the monosaccharide L-mannose; at the first carbon atom of this monosaccharide the configuration is $1\mathit{S}$ (L-mannose is the 2-epimer of L-glucose, and L-glucose in turn is the enantiomer of D-glucose);

give:

a) the open-chain (Fischer) formula of L-rhamnose (also give the line of reasoning);

b) the structural formula of the disodium salt of phosphoramidon, using three-dimensional formulae where necessary (Haworth formula, wedge-shaped bonds, dashed lines, etc.). Give the line of reasoning.

