b) wzór strukturalny soli disodowej fosforoamidonu, posługując się tam gdzie trzeba wzorami przestrzennymi (wzór Hawortha, wiązania w kształcie klina, linii przerywanych itp.). Podaj tok rozumowania.

problems.problem:
Problem 4. Structure of a disaccharide

Chitin is a polysaccharide occurring abundantly in nature in the exoskeletons of arthropods and in the cell walls or membranes of fungi and some protists and bacteria. The disaccharide fragment of chitin is chitobiose, which has the following elemental composition: $45.27\,\%$ C, $6.66\,\%$ H, $6.60\,\%$ N, $41.47\,\%$ O. Complete hydrolysis of the disaccharide gives, as the only reaction products, a monosaccharide $\mathbf{A}$ and acetic acid. On heating with ninhydrin, compound $\mathbf{A}$ gives a purple colour, whereas the analogous ninhydrin test with chitobiose is negative.

As a result of the following successive transformations of chitobiose:

$$\text{CHITOBIOSE} \xrightarrow[\text{methylation}]{\text{exhaustive}} \xrightarrow[\text{hydrolysis}]{\text{complete}} \xrightarrow{\text{reduction}} \mathbf{B^1} + \mathbf{C^1} \xrightarrow[\text{in water}]{\text{reaction with }\ce{HNO2}} \mathbf{B^2} + \mathbf{C^2}$$

two hexitol derivatives, $\mathbf{B^2}$ and $\mathbf{C^2}$, are obtained (besides insignificant by-products): 1,3,4-tri-$\textit{O}$-methylhexitol and 1,4-di-$\textit{O}$-methylhexitol (hexitol is hexane-1,2,3,4,5,6-hexaol).

Under the conditions of osazone formation (with phenylhydrazine), compound $\mathbf{A}$ forms an osazone identical with the osazone of D-glucose (and at the same time of D-mannose and D-fructose). The absolute configurations at carbon 2 and 5 in compound $\mathbf{A}$ are the same.

Both sugar rings in chitobiose are the same. Chitobiose is not hydrolysed by $\alpha$-glycosidase.

GIVE:

a) the molecular formula of chitobiose;

b) the structural formulae of 1,3,4-tri-$\textit{O}$-methylhexitol ($\mathbf{B^2}$) and 1,4-di-$\textit{O}$-methylhexitol ($\mathbf{C^2}$) - without regard to the configuration of the carbon atoms;

c) a scheme of the reaction giving a chosen hexitol derivative $\mathbf{B^2}$ or $\mathbf{C^2}$ from compound $\mathbf{B^1}$ or $\mathbf{C^1}$, taking into account the short-lived intermediate state;

d) the structural formula of the osazone of D-glucose (Fischer formula showing the configuration of the carbon atoms);

e) the Haworth or conformational (chair) structural formula of chitobiose;

f) a full description of the line of reasoning used in establishing the formula of chitobiose.

Note! For the calculations take the molar masses to the second decimal place

